## Interface: 16001, 120105
## Title: Social
## Notes: A chat window in the style of a messenger: every message in a bubble, yours on the right, everybody else's on the left with name and class icon. Enter or / opens the line to write in at its bottom, a click on the chat's name there lists the chats to write in. Move and size it in Edit Mode; push the mouse against the screen edge it is docked at and it fills the screen. The game's chat is out of sight while it is open and keeps every line; the setting Show the game's chat too keeps it on screen. /sane social (or /sane chat) hides this window.
## Author: Saneroki
## Version: 0.3.0
## Category: Sane UI
## Group: SaneUI
## Dependencies: SaneUI
## IconTexture: Interface\AddOns\SaneUI_Social\Art\icon
## X-License: MIT

# The module's own table, the game's chat events and the command. First: the other files add to that table.
Social.lua
# The messages: what an event says, and the list of them. Knows no frames
Log.lua
# Sizes and spacing, and what follows from a window's width. Knows no frames
Layout.lua
# The links in a message: tooltip and click
Links.lua
# How much of a message is seen: its own fade, kept on the message. Knows no frames
Fade.lua
# One message in the window
Bubble.lua
# Words picked out of the messages on the full screen, to copy with Ctrl+C
Select.lua
# Where you can write right now. Knows no frames
Channels.lua
# The conversations: every whisper, the party's, the raid's chat, each apart and kept. Knows no frames
Talks.lua
# The game's own chat: out of sight, and back
Native.lua
# The line you write in: the game's edit box, in our window
Input.lua
# The list behind the chat's name in that line: where to write, what to show, the game's channels
Menu.lua
# The smiley beside that line: raid marks to write, emotes to do
Picker.lua
# The game's own chat channels, the same on every character as wished. Knows no frames
Join.lua
# The full screen's parts: where they stand, the panels' look
Board.lua
# The guild window on the full screen: the one the guild key opens, held at its top right
Guild.lua
# The second chat of the full screen, in the conversations' list, with its own choice of chats
Feed.lua
# The friends list's panel of the full screen: what its lists share, you on Battle.net, then each list
Contacts\Contacts.lua
Contacts\Account.lua
Contacts\Friends.lua
Contacts\Requests.lua
Contacts\Ignored.lua
Contacts\Allies.lua
Contacts\Raid.lua
